--- RAST --->
CHECK: Module: [main]
// the *templates* dump first, and they are the before picture: a bare `T` with no upgrade in sight,
// which is correct - there is nothing to upgrade until something substitutes it
CHECK: function through_guard
CHECK: guard vardecl<type<Res>>($r) = varref<T>(var($w))
CHECK: function through_chain
CHECK: chainbase<T>
// then the instances, where the round that revealed the weak inserted the same node the parser would
// have. the upgraded handle is a value with no storage, so the ownership pass binds it to a temporary
// and releases it after - which is what keeps the count balanced
CHECK: function through_guard
CHECK: guard vardecl<type<Res>>($r) = strong<Res?>(varref<weak<Res>>(var($w)))
CHECK: function through_chain
CHECK: vardecl<type<Res?>>($__temp) = strong<Res?>(varref<weak<Res>>(var($w)))
// and the marker's stored type is the *unwrapped* one. cloning alone substitutes `T` into it and
// leaves `weak<Res>`, which is a handle nobody retained wearing the name of one that was
CHECK: ma<int32>(chainbase<Res>->tag)
CHECK: function through_coalesce
CHECK: coalesce<Res>(strong<Res?>(varref<weak<Res>>(var($w)))
